From: TB371FC entry reconstruction study
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] cpu: do not abort normal kexec for a suspend wake event

Base: tem423/android_kernel_lenovo_tb371fc
      9d8abebf4ac4d45cf4cc11b5b6bc5e4483d10fd1

kernel_kexec() sets kexec_in_progress before kernel_restart_prepare() and
machine_shutdown(). The arm64 machine_shutdown() calls
disable_nonboot_cpus(), reaching the vendor pm_wakeup_pending() abort in
freeze_secondary_cpus(). A pending suspend wakeup is not a reason to abandon
normal kexec's CPU teardown. Preserve the existing suspend behavior and
the context-preserving KEXEC_JUMP path, which does not set that flag here.

This does not suppress actual CPU-down errors or prove that every secondary
CPU can stop. It is newly reconstructed code, not the missing historic 0026.

--- a/kernel/cpu.c
+++ b/kernel/cpu.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <linux/export.h>
 #include <linux/bug.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
+#include <linux/kexec.h>
 #include <linux/stop_machine.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/gfp.h>
@@ -1355,7 +1356,7 @@
 		if (cpu == primary)
 			continue;
 
-		if (pm_wakeup_pending()) {
+		if (!kexec_in_progress && pm_wakeup_pending()) {
 			pr_info("Wakeup pending. Abort CPU freeze\n");
 			error = -EBUSY;
 			break;
